      "runtime": 80,
      "language": "ES",
      "synopsis_en": "At the end of the Spanish Civil War, almost half a million people moved by fear of reprisals to France. A hundred thousand of them were children. The French Government overflowed by the human avalanche, put them in improvised refugee camps. Chilean poet Pablo Neruda, former consul in Spain before the war, convinced the President of Chile to save more than two thousand refugees. The film tells the story of Julia, a little girl that escapes Barcelona with his father, a young widower. They embarked on the Winnipeg, a ship chartered by Neruda. That saved them from a dark future in Europe. Now, she is “a daughter of Neruda”, as the descendants of the 2,200 refugees call themselves.",
      "synopsis_zh": "1939 年，巴塞罗那被弗朗哥势力攻占，丧偶的父亲维克托带着小女儿胡莉亚离开西班牙。二人在法国身陷集中营，历经万般磨难。幸运的是，转机悄然出现，他们登上聂鲁达与巴黎贵格会租赁的货轮温尼伯号，乘船远赴智利瓦尔帕莱索，奔赴全新人生。",
